#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060523} :activity/id #uuid "6247c421-7779-51f5-a4bd-3cde04307793" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048362} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060523 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060892 :tutorial/content "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin (x+y) = \\sin x \\cos y + \\cos x \\sin y\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting $y= {\\color{blue}x}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(x+x) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x+\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}2x & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x+\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}2x & =2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equation above is called the **double-angle formula for sine**:\n\n$$\n\\sin 2x = 2 \\sin x \\cos x\n$$\n\nAs we will see, this formula has many applications. For instance, it allows us to simplify some trigonometric expressions and find the exact value of sine for some non-special angles.\n\nIt's important to realize that this is an identity, *not* an equation, which means that it is true for *all* values of $x.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "d14ca467-0ecd-5ac3-ab88-9bc2182a02ce" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2609 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "31a9aaf3-ced6-5bd9-a812-e8088d84003a" :step/math-academy-id 12230 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060524}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060524 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059671 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059499 :question/id #uuid "e95210c5-adb4-519e-bbec-e240dac32fd8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3614" :question/problem "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049773}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749367} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060399} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060402} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233278} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234047} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290560} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341901} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341926} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345251} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345252} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186695676} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186695678} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186695694} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696171} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696182} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696190} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696192} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696194} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696225} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696227} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696234} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696247} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696252} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696264} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749309} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749311} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749321} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749322} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749334} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749339} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749348} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749354} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749359} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749366}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"} :step/id #uuid "2697bac8-84d0-5fbd-ad5d-f33c14b3b3da" :step/math-academy-id 12231 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060526}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060525 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059672 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059500 :question/id #uuid "35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3618" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\right]\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749271} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060239} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060243} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233282} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233283} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253642} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253643} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290559} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290562} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290577} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302344} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323805} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323806} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345243} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345244} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696008} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696414} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696420} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696423} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696428} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696434} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696466} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696472} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696479} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696484} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749214} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749215} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749217} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749220} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749226} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749243} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749250} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749265} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749269}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"} :step/id #uuid "758d1a15-deaf-5a7d-a2b3-ab5cdc948bda" :step/math-academy-id 12270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060526 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059673 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059501 :question/id #uuid "b03496ac-c3b2-5d65-a3e3-2a33ea0cb862" :question/math-academy-id "e-3619" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡{25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050928}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696372} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060241} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060242} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233279} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234181} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253627} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253628} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253629} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253630} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253632} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253633} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290558} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335849} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335850} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335851} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335852} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696347} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696353} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696356} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696369} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696456} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696490} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696500}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"} :step/id #uuid "2e2b09a9-557f-5799-9a72-622f4f3713d3" :step/math-academy-id 12275 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060527}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060527 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059674 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059502 :question/id #uuid "539b5b86-7b31-52c9-be04-e80d6799b68a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3623" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle 3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by $\\dfrac 1 2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)} } = 3 \\left( \\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749296} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060249} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060398} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233280} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253634} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253636} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290576} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292685} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302330} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302332} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302347} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345239} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345240} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696379} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696380} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696386} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696405} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696501} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696509} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749284} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749285} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749293}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"} :step/id #uuid "6c628c14-aae8-5b84-9c12-e5b22b1018e6" :step/math-academy-id 12302 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060525}}] :activity/title "The Double-Angle Formula for Sine" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059946}]}
